<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:57Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Russia's Vladimir Putin suggests no Ukraine compromise in meeting with US envoys</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d82d4c874d263b3e07136d43cc9f7f7dc4ca7724daa3e1daa0aa6db5cf27fde</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T16:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys--26ef97037a98.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-russia-s-vladimir-putin-suggests-no-ukraine-compromise-in-meeting-with-us-envoys" /><summary type="html">Russia's President Vladimir Putin indicated on Thursday, November 12, that the Kremlin would not compromise on its hardline demands to end the war in Ukraine, but offered a short-term ceasefire in a key frontline city during a meeting with US envoys. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Philip Turle has more.</summary></entry><entry><title>France: Five men on trial for murder of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci's brother</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4d094a78bb4133f8a12685928e33a8ff4f2c88f91d8715678501a0330912e44</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:55:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T14:20:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother--97c5322846e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-france-five-men-on-trial-for-murder-of-anti-drug-activist-amine-kessaci-s-brother" /><summary type="html">In France, the trial of five men accused of murdering the brother of anti-drug activist Amine Kessaci is under way. Amine Kessaci, originally known as an environmental activist, became a prominent figure in the fight against drug-related crime after losing two of his brothers to violence linked to drug trafficking. The defendants face the possibility of life imprisonment. The verdict is expected on Monday, November 16. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>European leaders gather in Dublin to discuss Ukraine's security, and their own</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b32bcd15c2077427f2717f221ac5f2f66c64597ce049016c9f9f9585e5a8b7b</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:19:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own--56692e996cbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-to-discuss-ukraine-s-security-and-their-own" /><summary type="html">Leaders from more than 40 European countries gathered in Dublin on Thursday, November 12, for a summit focused on the continent’s fragile security, amid a new US-backed effort to revive talks on ending the Russia-Ukraine war. The meeting of the European Political Community brought together heads of state and government from European countries and the UK, as well as Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney and NATO Secretary-General Mark Rutte.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands of schools evacuated in Italy as bomb threats spread across Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ebee3cc6ef75a3cb782cd682e2157efb62fe7e9c12689cd31175baaf6c26d860</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:08:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe--85c832b8d0d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-thousands-of-schools-evacuated-in-italy-as-bomb-threats-spread-across-europe" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". The threats come after a series of hoax bomb alerts across Europe in recent weeks, which have prompted growing concern about the possibility of an escalation in hybrid warfare.</summary></entry><entry><title>COP31: Climate disruption puts farmers and global food supplies under pressure</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c448a44a1ba2b590a4685c7421640388e2d89874d492b593f6c7f590ec073b59</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T11:04:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure--703bcb8d3e50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261112-cop31-climate-disruption-puts-farmers-and-global-food-supplies-under-pressure" /><summary type="html">As delegates gather in Turkey for the COP31 climate conference, discussions are focusing on emissions and climate targets. But humanitarian agencies are highlighting another urgent consequence of climate disruption: growing food insecurity. With the return of El Niño adding to concerns over extreme weather and its impact on food production, the Food and Agriculture Organisation is calling for food systems to be placed at the heart of climate action.</summary></entry><entry><title>New restrictions to Starshield network 'kill more Ukrainians', Zelensky says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6718f613c20ec22b354116b2fd28d7ca24b4e34a31ec5c3220b57d5a31a467f4</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:55Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T10:06:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says--b63c57dc57ec.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-new-systematic-restrictions-starshield-network-kill-more-ukrainians-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian ⁠President Volodymyr Zelensky ​on Thursday said that Ukrainian ​military units had recorded new and significant disruptions to the Starshield satellite communications service in recent days, affecting ​the ‌entire front ⁠line and Russian-occupied parts of Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia's 'hidden mobilization': The 'expendable' lives fueling Putin's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94564427e4b20c34de21898fc4f3a195ad5182ff9c502b1291d87a6f15596277</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:56:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T07:39:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-s-hidden-mobilization-the-expendable-lives-fueling-putin-s-war-on-ukraine--f5e8509ede95.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-s-hidden-mobilization-the-expendable-lives-fueling-putin-s-war-on-ukraine" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome John Lough, Senior Research Fellow and Head of Foreign Policy &amp; International Partnerships at the New Eurasian Strategies Centre (NEST Centre), He is also an Associate Fellow with the Russia &amp; Eurasia Programme at Chatham House. Lough offers a sobering assessment of the social and strategic dynamics sustaining Russia's invasion of Ukraine. He argues that the Kremlin has disproportionately recruited soldiers from poorer and politically marginalised communities, including ethnic minority regions, where the human cost of the conflict is less likely to generate organised opposition. Many of those recruited, he explains, "have been recruited for a deliberate reason because they were seen, you know, ultimately as lives that were expendable, in other words as cannon fodder."</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Putin offers to evacuate civilians from Ukraine's Kostiantynivka after Oleshky truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b95bc34f5177a00dc7e6f58740b0a142a3a94668bdc5db3dbde628e227c5a42e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T02:31:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks--eb0f36381594.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261112-live-us-envoys-to-meet-putin-and-zelensky-after-abu-dhabi-talks" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir ​Putin on Thursday told ​US envoys that Moscow was proposing a joint Russian-Ukrainian humanitarian ​mission ‌to the ⁠city of Kostiantynivka in eastern ‌Ukraine, the Interfax news agency reported. He said the mission could be modelled on the brief truce that allowed residents to leave the Russia-controlled town of Oleshky in October. Follow our liveblog for live updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>European leaders gather in Dublin under the shadow of hybrid threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2d042f82b3c2c8e3ec85fa5e81a4115e91a359dbcb471973f9b887bc3beec54</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T22:46:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-under-the-shadow-of-hybrid-threats--ebbc2bf82ef8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/european-leaders-gather-in-dublin-under-the-shadow-of-hybrid-threats" /><summary type="html">Ireland is mounting the largest security operation in its history as around 50 European leaders gather in Dublin this week amid growing concerns over hybrid attacks. The operation follows a wave of hoax bomb threats targeting airlines and media organisations across Europe, with Irish police reporting new incidents on Monday and Tuesday. FRANCE 24's Olivia Bizot reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia and Ukraine agree to major prisoner swap as peace talks end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73ea7d20644d17652adbed937c2bf79cd0a68204c4ed2d9072a5b056d2def80e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:46:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end--e9c04d147348.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-and-ukraine-agree-to-major-prisoner-swap-as-peace-talks-end" /><summary type="html">Kyiv and Moscow on Wednesday agreed to a large-scale prisoner exchange as the final day of peace talks in Abu Dhabi came to an end, though neither side gave a concrete figure. US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner will meet separately with Russian President Vladimir Putin and his Ukrainian counterpart Volodymyr Zelensky on Thursday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out hundreds of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1c1b83f6570adbf54b3f7e6b861427a3857b611787b96ee5a55d5f6d512c88c2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:31:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain--305c14ca2c0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-hundreds-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Millions of workers in Spain shut down businesses and public transport on Wednesday, as part of the country's first general strike in 14 years. Following a peaceful march in Barcelona over soaring rents and property prices, and the rising cost of living, protesters smashed storefronts, set off small bonfires, burned bins and launched fireworks towards police. The unrest comes just weeks before snap elections, called by Socialist Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>General strike over housing brings out tens of thousands in Spain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ac505c8d44b6d72debb0d222f1e6c7e0245020c80a84edaf9d029b8b3034120</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:37:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain--b3f1fe2dfc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/general-strike-over-housing-brings-out-tens-of-thousands-in-spain" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of protesters marched across Spain on Wednesday during a general strike over housing affordability and purchasing power just weeks before an early general election. Unions reported a significant response in some sectors in Spain's first nationwide 24-hour stoppage since 2012, but business leaders played down the participation. Braving heavy rain, tens of thousands of demonstrators marched through central Madrid carrying placards shaped like houses and chanting "We have no home" as they called for more affordable housing. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days after shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26cf7eb5579450e4b987814faafc4f23c2b64a8166d938dc989d027ab4cd9382</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:31:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1--6aff4f4e4234.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings-1" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. The event is a magnet for all shades of Poland's right wing -- from conservative-nationalists aligned with its Law and Justice (PiS) party to far-right and radical groups. FRANCE 24's Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Schools evacuated across Italy after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6d8482cad6708a45fb02d0ad0200e516316f431471272f2ca994fcc8a5a12264</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:29:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats--8b8597a1d133.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/schools-evacuated-across-italy-after-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Schools were evacuated across Italy on Wednesday following a series of hoax bomb threats, but Italian Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni said there was no "concrete danger". Similar hoax threats were reported in schools in Britain and Ireland, which reportedly prompted some evacuations in Scotland. Meloni said she had called a government meeting with security and intelligence chiefs for Wednesday to discuss the threats. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands attend Polish nationalist march days afer shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b02bb5617a9cacae30e52e36b350396e5ed74669bc084092ccbb20ebf7323c57</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:08:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings--f224bca0510d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-attend-polish-nationalist-march-days-afer-shootings" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of Polish nationalist sympathisers gathered in Warsaw Wednesday for an annual Independence Day March, just days after a deadly shooting spree in Krakow that shook the country. The event is held each November 11 to commemorate the ending in 1918 of 123 years of partition by Russia, Prussia and Austria. While generally peaceful, some rallies in the pasthave been marred by clashes with police or counter-demonstrators. Philip Turle gives us his take.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia bans two French lawmakers and two journalists from entry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3645f23b949e5bc35b9ff59d723b04707705de8416eb15738a1da3b827e00a3a</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:58:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry--647f8165ba44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-russia-bans-two-french-lawmakers-and-two-journalists-from-entry" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Wednesday said it was banning two French journalists and two French lawmakers from entering Russia in response to Paris's expulsion of pro-Russian TV commentator Xenia Fedorova earlier this year.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Spain: General strike over housing costs before national election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb3193d49677c1258d7fd8ac5ef775068b856733bbcf7d868037cb8948a6b59</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:54:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election--d795ce513ad5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-general-strike-over-housing-costs-before-national-election" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers shut down businesses and public transportation in a protest on Wednesday over housing costs that the government hopes to leverage before a national election later this month. The walkout — under the slogan “Salaries. Housing. Prices.” — was the first general strike in Spain in 14 years.</summary></entry><entry><title>Exclusive: EU's Kallas says US 'can't negotiate on our behalf' on lifting Russia sanctions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5cd1af68f3cdb0f5d05a0445cb946836d6eda17c84a91c22b66109f848ec4089</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:15:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions--7f31e05dcc4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261111-exclusive-eu-s-kallas-says-us-can-t-negotiate-on-our-behalf-on-lifting-russia-sanctions" /><summary type="html">In an exclusive interview with FRANCE 24, the EU's top diplomat Kaja Kallas discusses the war in Ukraine, the situation in the Middle East and a possible change in US President Donald Trump's foreign policy following the US midterm elections. The former Estonian prime minister, who is now the European Union's High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy, also reaffirms the EU's position as a major player on the global geopolitical stage.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Aneto, one of southern Europe's largest glaciers, is melting away</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa30a57158ee59afa925cf839d2bc4afa8ba8022456bae626ac82fba7bd3adf0</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away--7bca17aca8fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261111-aneto-one-of-southern-europe-s-largest-glaciers-is-melting-away" /><summary type="html">Within a decade, one of the largest glaciers in southern Europe will have disappeared. Aneto, the highest peak of the Spanish Pyrenees, is melting at a spectacular rate. Its demise is another sign of global warming and has much to teach glaciologists. FRANCE 24's Maude Petit-Jové, Mathilde Lopinski and Sarah Morris report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Patrick Bury: 'It’s going to cost a lot of money to repair the systems.'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcee0fe3f07068638c0254e493d574514ad674bf6256673a7fcfbb3d11415c6e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T12:32:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict--d7020f165247.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-how-prepared-is-the-continent-to-face-a-futur-conflict" /><summary type="html">Patrick Bury, Senior associate professor in warfare and counterterrorism at University of Bath, is our guest.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK comedian David Walliams accused of grooming and sexual harassment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2960c932574a6ab6fa0c25fa8ad3d07e122f495347b4ce0c31083eebec55b3d9</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:56:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment--5fccf1ffbe7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261111-uk-comedian-david-walliams-accused-of-grooming-and-sexual-harassment" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, November 11: Spanish and French papers discuss protests in the two countries. An investigation by The Guardian and ITV accuses comedian David Walliams of "preying on young women for sex". Finally, a Doberman sensed something was wrong with a baby. It may have saved his life.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Wave of hoax bomb threats sent to schools in UK, Ireland and Italy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c421b94824203a5ee75a701e69d75c0808a06262210c1f4f677ff3f08a6020df</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:57:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats--967169548911.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-hundreds-of-schools-in-italy-evacuated-after-receiving-bomb-threats" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of schools in the UK, Italy and the Republic of Ireland received a "generic" threatening email on Wednesday now being treated as a hoax by authorities. Italy earlier evacuated roughly 300 schools over the perceived threat.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Russia, Ukraine start second day of US-led talks: Kyiv lead negotiator</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1246e7ad910c733a83f704901d5748ec4611e89bec9e9b46d4c1facc3fdb744c</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:42:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator--ce553d61579f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-ukraine-start-second-day-of-us-led-talks-kyiv-lead-negotiator" /><summary type="html">Russia and Ukraine have resumed US-mediated talks in Abu Dhabi for a second day, Kyiv's chief negotiator Rustem Umerov said on Wednesday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain's first general strike in 14 years, 3 weeks before national polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5617c5cb45c0f03ee54227cda0f351a34a6a6b721f09e8fda497b30af1e547a3</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:30:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/spain-s-first-general-strike-in-14-years-3-weeks-before-national-polls--7baf50b0712f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/spain-s-first-general-strike-in-14-years-3-weeks-before-national-polls" /><summary type="html">Sarah Morris is live from Madrid.</summary></entry><entry><title>Portugal shuts schools, tech conference as it braces for storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c960b0a11201c96445c9bceaf87b85d7d5011b7a0261c26d301f33361dd8f77e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T10:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/portugal-shuts-schools-tech-conference-as-it-braces-for-storm--85bdf5a4749a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/portugal-shuts-schools-tech-conference-as-it-braces-for-storm" /><summary type="html">Portugal said it would shut schools, non-essential services and a top world tech conference on Wednesday, as it braces for gale-force winds of Storm Charles.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK authorities arrest US soldier suspected of spying for Russia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:195cca878194c28162841644d4c98ab589ec1e116720d70b6a2b2316772fa0aa</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T09:41:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-authorities-arrests-us-soldier-suspected-of-spying-for-russia--305fec5257b9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-authorities-arrests-us-soldier-suspected-of-spying-for-russia" /><summary type="html">A member of the US army suspected of spying for Russia was arrested in Britain on Tuesday, London police said, following an investigation with support from the American military and law enforcement.</summary></entry><entry><title>Spain’s general strike puts housing crisis at centre of upcoming elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dff9aee7a47dba181819f55e85e0742d5ab4e9a07eb3ddcf9153293eeff89dcf</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T08:29:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-spain-general-strike-puts-housing-crisis-centre-upcoming-elections--d80411702cc0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-spain-general-strike-puts-housing-crisis-centre-upcoming-elections" /><summary type="html">Millions of Spanish workers are striking Wednesday – the first general strike in 14 years – to demand action on a major housing crisis and the rising cost of living. The expected disruptions to public transport and the widespread closure of businesses come less than three weeks before a snap election that could bring the far right to power.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Abu Dhabi peace talks show US, Europe and Ukraine are ‘aligned’, NATO chief says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7fcb196a08ad31c11f6893e8c5e39d455beb68c8ddaa53e410fbb08421bd94f2</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T03:22:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-live-ukraine-russia-hold-second-day-of-us-mediated-talks-in-abu-dhabi--18813df16781.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261111-live-ukraine-russia-hold-second-day-of-us-mediated-talks-in-abu-dhabi" /><summary type="html">The US-mediated Ukraine-Russia peace talks in Abu Dhabi showed that the US, Ukraine and Europe were "aligned and united", NATO Secretary General Mark Rutte said Wednesday. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky arrived in Dublin Wednesday evening to meet European leaders and US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner following the negotiations. Read our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Europe not going anywhere': G7 summit a 'signal to Russians' that Europe is standing behind Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e43efc7b2980a1cc8e91b62eca34d2e8e508e911500f0892a3122833d9506716</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe-not-going-anywhere-g7-summit-a-signal-to-russians-that-europe-is-standing-behind-ukraine--7a75adc507db.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe-not-going-anywhere-g7-summit-a-signal-to-russians-that-europe-is-standing-behind-ukraine" /><summary type="html">As the US Midterms reshape Ukraine diplomacy, Annette Young is pleased to welcome James Townsend, Atlantic Council's Senior Advisor at the Scowcroft Center's for Transatlantic Security Initiative. "Europe is not going anywhere." With this unequivocal assessment, Townsend, taking place alongside trilateral negotiations in Abu Dhabi. While the latter may command international attention, Townsend argues that the Paris meeting carries a message of its own: European support for Ukraine is intended to remain durable, and Moscow should not mistake diplomatic negotiations for an erosion of Western resolve. The G7 meeting therefore emerges as more than a forum for diplomatic declarations. It represents a test of Western cohesion, the credibility of future military and financial assistance, and Washington's willingness to endorse a common position on Ukraine. As Townsend emphasizes, the final communiqué will also be "a test as far as what Marco Rubio is going to agree to put his name to."</summary></entry><entry><title>Asymmetric cyberwarfare: 'States increasingly use cyberattacks in support of their other objectives'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8df99d4cbee983353ffaca7bdd7483bb21473d1b4eda74b6ce73a0945ee5ba2e</id><updated>2026-11-12T16:54:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T21:25:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives--937e2d10d52d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Rafe Pilling, Director of Threat Intelligence in the Sophos Counter Threat Unit (CTU). How can a minor cyber intrusion disrupt food supplies, expose the weaknesses of industrial infrastructure and become an instrument of geopolitical confrontation? The cyberattacks targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in France offer a revealing illustration of how digital vulnerabilities can translate into tangible economic disruption and potentially broader threats to society. As Pilling explains, “With a small amount of effort from the adversary side, they can create a large impact, in this case destroying food and producing empty shelves or empty refrigeration units in stores.” This asymmetry lies at the heart of contemporary cyber conflict, in which modest technical interventions can produce disproportionate economic and operational consequences</summary></entry></feed>
